{
  "info": {
    "name": "Rescue Alert System — Production",
    "description": "Production API reference for the Rescue Alert System.\n\n## Authentication\nThe API uses Django REST Framework SimpleJWT. Protected endpoints require the access token returned by this API:\n```\nAuthorization: Bearer <access_token>\n```\n\n**Quick start:**\n1. Set `user_email` and `user_password` in collection variables.\n2. If needed, run **Authentication → Register**. This creates a Django user and saves the returned token pair.\n3. Run **Authentication → Login (Obtain Tokens)**. It automatically saves `access` and `refresh` into `access_token` and `refresh_token`.\n4. Run **Authentication → Verify Current Token** before testing protected endpoints.\n\nUse **Authentication → Refresh Access Token** when an access token expires. Firebase ID tokens are not accepted by this API.\n\n## Variables\n| Variable | Description |\n|---|---|\n| `base_url` | Production API base URL |\n| `user_email` | Django username/email used to register or sign in |\n| `user_password` | Django account password |\n| `access_token` | JWT access token — auto-set by Register, Login, and Refresh |\n| `refresh_token` | JWT refresh token — auto-set by Register and Login |\n| `alert_id` | Alert ID for detail/update/delete requests |\n| `user_id` | UserProfile ID for detail/update/delete requests |\n| `group_id` | Group ID for detail/update/delete requests |\n| `message_id` | Message ID for detail/update/delete requests |\n| `notification_id` | Notification token record ID |\n\n## Notes\n- `POST /api/auth/register/` creates the Django account; it is not created implicitly by a Firebase request.\n- `sender` on messages and `user` on notifications are set automatically from the authenticated Django user; do not include them in request bodies.\n- `voice_file` uploads use `multipart/form-data`; do not set `Content-Type` manually — Postman adds the boundary automatically.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
